.TH SCREENCATCH 1 "October 2026" "ScreenCatch 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
screencatch \- take a screenshot and annotate it instantly
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B screencatch
[\fIOPTION\fR...] [\fIIMAGE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B screencatch
captures the screen through the XDG desktop screenshot portal, lets you select a
region over the frozen screen and opens an editor to add arrows, rectangles,
ellipses, lines, freehand pen and highlighter strokes, text, numbered steps and
pixelation. The result can be copied to the clipboard or saved as a PNG file.
.PP
Run without options, it starts a region capture immediately; bind it to a key
for the quickest workflow. On GNOME the shortcut Ctrl+Shift+Print is registered
automatically on first start and can be changed in Preferences.
.PP
When images are given, they are opened in the editor instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-full
Capture the whole screen and open it in the editor.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delay =\fISECONDS\fR
Wait \fISECONDS\fR before capturing.
.TP
.B \-\-home
Show the main window instead of capturing.
.TP
.B \-\-preferences
Open the preferences.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print debug messages.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help options.
.SH SELECTION KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
Run the quick action (open the editor by default).
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Copy the selected region to the clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save the selected region to the screenshot folder.
.TP
.B Space
Select the whole monitor.
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel.
.SH FILES
Screenshots are saved to
.I ~/Pictures/Screenshots
unless another folder is configured.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/sholehbaktiabadi/screencatch/issues
